  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "Here, $9$ raised to the power of $3$ means ${9}^{3}.$\n\nTo compute this power, we start by writing it out with multiplication signs:\n\n$$\n{9}^{3}={{9\\times 9\\times 9}_{⏟}}_{3\\text{ times}}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the product. Since $9\\times 9=81,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{{9\\times 9}_{⏟}}_{81}\\times 9 & =81\\times 9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we work out $81\\times 9.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned} &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,{}_{}\\,\\,\\,\\, &  \\\\  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,8\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,\\times \\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,9\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,7\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,9\\,\\,\\,\\,\\end{aligned} \\\\  & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $81\\times 9=729,$ then ${9}^{3}=729.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
